1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,145
Imagine you put

2
00:00:01,145 --> 00:00:02,697
$1,000 in the bank.

3
00:00:02,857 --> 00:00:04,266
You think it just sits there,

4
00:00:04,266 --> 00:00:05,267
waiting for you, right?

5
00:00:05,427 --> 00:00:07,283
Well, that's not exactly what happens!

6
00:00:07,703 --> 00:00:09,720
Banks use money from deposits

7
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:10,583
to help make loans.

8
00:00:10,743 --> 00:00:13,477
For example, a family might borrow money

9
00:00:13,477 --> 00:00:14,690
from the bank to buy a house.

10
00:00:15,110 --> 00:00:16,552
But borrowing isn't free!

11
00:00:16,552 --> 00:00:18,971
The bank charges something called interest.

12
00:00:19,131 --> 00:00:21,048
If you borrow $1,000

13
00:00:21,048 --> 00:00:23,138
at 8% interest for one year,

14
00:00:23,138 --> 00:00:24,977
that's $80 in interest.

15
00:00:25,397 --> 00:00:27,137
Now imagine your savings account

16
00:00:27,137 --> 00:00:28,853
pays 1% interest.

17
00:00:29,013 --> 00:00:30,937
You earn just $10 in a year

18
00:00:30,937 --> 00:00:32,149
on your $1,000.

19
00:00:32,309 --> 00:00:34,719
Meanwhile, the bank earns interest from borrowers.

20
00:00:35,139 --> 00:00:37,675
Banks can also earn money from investments,

21
00:00:37,675 --> 00:00:38,937
like government bonds.

22
00:00:39,097 --> 00:00:40,344
And some banks charge fees

23
00:00:40,344 --> 00:00:43,542
for helping customers invest in mutual funds,

24
00:00:43,542 --> 00:00:45,774
which are baskets of investments.

25
00:00:46,194 --> 00:00:48,669
Now imagine millions of customers doing this!

26
00:00:48,829 --> 00:00:50,386
That's how banks can make billions.

27
00:00:50,546 --> 00:00:52,409
Of course, they also pay expenses,

28
00:00:52,409 --> 00:00:54,023
and sometimes lose money.

29
00:00:54,183 --> 00:00:55,035
So remember:

30
00:00:55,035 --> 00:00:57,277
banks work to earn money using deposits.

31
00:00:57,437 --> 00:00:59,058
Are you making the most of yours?

